      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e fsfdt change wouldn\u0027t be necessary if all of following happens \n\nfsfdt change is for fixing the bug. I believe `append()` should be able to cope with existing subnode in the target DT.\n \n\n\u003e loading from path comes before untrusted props appending\n\nThat maybe tricky. It does sound like a hack to avoid hitting the bug. What flow will create the `/avf/` subnode in target tree?\n1) If `append()` adds it (because Path was present \u0026 was called before adding untrusted props), then we will not explicitly call `add_subnode(AVF_NODE_NAME)` [line 80].\n2) If the path is not present, then we will need to keep this around.\n\nwhich only adds complexity to this method to avoid a bug.\n\n\n\u003e create_device_tree_overlay(buffer: \u0026mut [u8], base_fs_dir: \u0026Path, untrusted_props: \u0026[(\u0026Cstr, \u0026[u8])])\n\nBut path `base_fs_dir` may not be present if reference DT is not preset on host DT. Even if we change it to `create_device_tree_overlay(buffer: \u0026mut [u8], base_fs_dir: \u0026Option\u003cPath\u003e, untrusted_props: \u0026[(\u0026Cstr, \u0026[u8])])`, I dont see the advantage of it over (what I think) is a cleared encapsulation of `DtAddition`",
